IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ssc-core`
IMPORT `ssc1-prelim`

-- Tests for ssc1-prelim.l4 (ss 1 to 4C). Every expected value is written from the text, beside the assertion.
-- Fixtures are named `ssc1 fixture ...` so that no other part can define the same name.

§ `Tests for ss 1 to 4C`

`ssc1 fixture person` MEANS Person WITH
    `date of birth` IS Date 1 1 1990
    `sex` IS Woman
    `marital status` IS `neither married nor in a civil partnership`
    `date of attaining pensionable age` IS Date 1 1 2056

-- employed under a contract of service in Great Britain
`ssc1 fixture contract of service in GB` MEANS Employment WITH
    `the employee` IS `ssc1 fixture person`
    `the kind of employer` IS `a company or other body corporate`
    `the employment began on` IS Date 1 4 2020
    `the employment ended on` IS NOTHING
    `held under a contract of service` IS TRUE
    `held in an office` IS FALSE
    `carried on in Great Britain` IS TRUE

-- holder of an office, in Great Britain
`ssc1 fixture office in GB` MEANS Employment WITH
    `the employee` IS `ssc1 fixture person`
    `the kind of employer` IS `a government department, public authority or other body of persons`
    `the employment began on` IS Date 1 4 2020
    `the employment ended on` IS NOTHING
    `held under a contract of service` IS FALSE
    `held in an office` IS TRUE
    `carried on in Great Britain` IS TRUE

-- neither a contract of service nor an office: self-employment, in Great Britain
`ssc1 fixture own business in GB` MEANS Employment WITH
    `the employee` IS `ssc1 fixture person`
    `the kind of employer` IS `an individual`
    `the employment began on` IS Date 1 4 2020
    `the employment ended on` IS NOTHING
    `held under a contract of service` IS FALSE
    `held in an office` IS FALSE
    `carried on in Great Britain` IS TRUE

-- under a contract of service, but not carried on in Great Britain
`ssc1 fixture contract of service abroad` MEANS Employment WITH
    `the employee` IS `ssc1 fixture person`
    `the kind of employer` IS `a company or other body corporate`
    `the employment began on` IS Date 1 4 2020
    `the employment ended on` IS NOTHING
    `held under a contract of service` IS TRUE
    `held in an office` IS FALSE
    `carried on in Great Britain` IS FALSE

§§ `s 1`

-- s 1(1): the two purposes named in (a) and (b) are provided for by contributions; another purpose is not covered.
#ASSERT `s 1(1) the funds are to be provided by means of contributions payable to the Inland Revenue` `s 1(1)(a) paying benefits payable out of the National Insurance Fund and not out of other public money` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1(1) the funds are to be provided by means of contributions payable to the Inland Revenue` `s 1(1)(b) payments under section 162 of the Administration Act towards the cost of the National Health Service` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1(1) the funds are to be provided by means of contributions payable to the Inland Revenue` `s 1(1) a purpose the text does not name` EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 1(2): the eight classes. Expected strings are the text's own words (src:10-18).
#ASSERT (`s 1(2) the description of the class` `Class 1 primary`)'s `s 1(2) the sections it is payable under` EQUALS "section 6"
#ASSERT (`s 1(2) the description of the class` `Class 1 primary`)'s `s 1(2) who pays it` EQUALS "employed earners"
#ASSERT (`s 1(2) the description of the class` `Class 1 secondary`)'s `s 1(2) who pays it` EQUALS "employers and other persons paying earnings"
#ASSERT (`s 1(2) the description of the class` `Class 1A`)'s `s 1(2) the sections it is payable under` EQUALS "section 10"
#ASSERT (`s 1(2) the description of the class` `Class 1B`)'s `s 1(2) the sections it is payable under` EQUALS "section 10A"
#ASSERT (`s 1(2) the description of the class` `Class 2`)'s `s 1(2) who pays it` EQUALS "self-employed earners"
#ASSERT (`s 1(2) the description of the class` `Class 2`)'s `s 1(2) what it is` EQUALS "Class 2, flat-rate"
#ASSERT (`s 1(2) the description of the class` `Class 3`)'s `s 1(2) the sections it is payable under` EQUALS "section 13 or 13A"
#ASSERT (`s 1(2) the description of the class` `Class 3A`)'s `s 1(2) the sections it is payable under` EQUALS "section 14A"
#ASSERT (`s 1(2) the description of the class` `Class 4`)'s `s 1(2) the sections it is payable under` EQUALS "section 15 or section 18"

-- s 1(4): Schedule 1 has effect for Classes 1, 1A, 1B, 3 and 3A; Class 2 (gap in the list) and Class 4 (only as regulations provide) are not covered.
#ASSERT `s 1(4) Schedule 1 has effect with respect to the computation, collection and recovery of the class` `Class 1 primary` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1(4) Schedule 1 has effect with respect to the computation, collection and recovery of the class` `Class 1 secondary` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1(4) Schedule 1 has effect with respect to the computation, collection and recovery of the class` `Class 1A` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1(4) Schedule 1 has effect with respect to the computation, collection and recovery of the class` `Class 1B` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1(4) Schedule 1 has effect with respect to the computation, collection and recovery of the class` `Class 3` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1(4) Schedule 1 has effect with respect to the computation, collection and recovery of the class` `Class 3A` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 1(4) Schedule 1 has effect with respect to the computation, collection and recovery of the class` `Class 2` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 1(4) Schedule 1 has effect with respect to the computation, collection and recovery of the class` `Class 4` EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 1(5): the addition equals the aggregate of the seven statutory payments recovered: 1+2+3+4+5+6+7 = 28.
`ssc1 fixture recovered` MEANS `s 1(5) Statutory payments recovered in a financial year` OF 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7
#ASSERT `s 1(5) the total of the amounts to be paid out of money provided by Parliament for the year` `ssc1 fixture recovered` EQUALS 28

-- s 1(6)(a): not fulfilling the prescribed conditions bars Classes 1 (both), 1A, 1B and 2; fulfilling them does not make the person liable.
#ASSERT `s 1(6)(a) the person is liable to pay a Class 1, Class 1A, Class 1B or Class 2 contribution` `Class 1 primary` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 1(6)(a) the person is liable to pay a Class 1, Class 1A, Class 1B or Class 2 contribution` `Class 1 secondary` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 1(6)(a) the person is liable to pay a Class 1, Class 1A, Class 1B or Class 2 contribution` `Class 1A` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 1(6)(a) the person is liable to pay a Class 1, Class 1A, Class 1B or Class 2 contribution` `Class 1B` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 1(6)(a) the person is liable to pay a Class 1, Class 1A, Class 1B or Class 2 contribution` `Class 2` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 1(6)(a) the person is liable to pay a Class 1, Class 1A, Class 1B or Class 2 contribution` `Class 2` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 1(6)(a) the person is liable to pay a Class 1, Class 1A, Class 1B or Class 2 contribution` `Class 3` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 1(6)(a) the person is liable to pay a Class 1, Class 1A, Class 1B or Class 2 contribution` `Class 4` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 1(6)(aa), (b)
#ASSERT `s 1(6)(aa) the person is treated under section 11(5B) as having actually paid Class 2 contributions` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 1(6)(aa) the person is treated under section 11(5B) as having actually paid Class 2 contributions` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 1(6)(b) the person is entitled to pay Class 3 contributions` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 1(6)(b) the person is entitled to pay Class 3 contributions` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 1(6)(c): a contribution the person is not liable to pay, and no permission by regulations, is barred; permission or liability lifts the bar
#ASSERT `s 1(6)(c) the person is entitled to pay a Class 1, Class 1A, Class 1B or Class 2 contribution` `Class 2` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 1(6)(c) the person is entitled to pay a Class 1, Class 1A, Class 1B or Class 2 contribution` `Class 1A` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 1(6)(c) the person is entitled to pay a Class 1, Class 1A, Class 1B or Class 2 contribution` `Class 2` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 1(6)(c) the person is entitled to pay a Class 1, Class 1A, Class 1B or Class 2 contribution` `Class 2` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 1(6)(c) the person is entitled to pay a Class 1, Class 1A, Class 1B or Class 2 contribution` `Class 4` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `s 2`

-- s 2(1)(a): employed earner. Contract of service in GB, gainfully employed: yes.
#ASSERT `s 2(1)(a) the person is an employed earner` `ssc1 fixture contract of service in GB` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- an office in GB with earnings: yes; an office without earnings: no
#ASSERT `s 2(1)(a) the person is an employed earner` `ssc1 fixture office in GB` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2(1)(a) the person is an employed earner` `ssc1 fixture office in GB` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- not gainfully employed: no; not in Great Britain: no; neither a contract nor an office: no
#ASSERT `s 2(1)(a) the person is an employed earner` `ssc1 fixture contract of service in GB` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 2(1)(a) the person is an employed earner` `ssc1 fixture contract of service abroad` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 2(1)(a) the person is an employed earner` `ssc1 fixture own business in GB` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 2(1)(b): self-employed earner: gainfully employed in GB otherwise than in employed earner's employment
#ASSERT `s 2(1)(b) the person is a self-employed earner` `ssc1 fixture own business in GB` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2(1)(b) the person is a self-employed earner` `ssc1 fixture contract of service in GB` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 2(1)(b) the person is a self-employed earner` `ssc1 fixture own business in GB` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 2(1)(b) the person is a self-employed earner` `ssc1 fixture office in GB` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- s 2(2ZB): arrangements include the four named; something else is not covered
#ASSERT `s 2(2ZB) the thing is an arrangement` `s 2(2ZB) a scheme` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2(2ZB) the thing is an arrangement` `s 2(2ZB) a transaction or series of transactions` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2(2ZB) the thing is an arrangement` `s 2(2ZB) an agreement or understanding` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2(2ZB) the thing is an arrangement` `s 2(2ZB) associated operations` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2(2ZB) the thing is an arrangement` `s 2(2ZB) something else` EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 2(3)
#ASSERT `s 2(3) the person is treated as an employed earner for all purposes of this Act` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2(3) the person is treated as an employed earner for all purposes of this Act` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 2(4): section 95's answer governs when it says yes; otherwise (1) to (3), with section 95 outside the text
#ASSERT `s 2(4) the employment is employed earner's employment for the purposes of industrial injuries benefit` (JUST FALSE) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2(4) the employment is employed earner's employment for the purposes of industrial injuries benefit` (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2(4) the employment is employed earner's employment for the purposes of industrial injuries benefit` (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 2(4) the employment is employed earner's employment for the purposes of industrial injuries benefit` (JUST FALSE) NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 2(4) the employment is employed earner's employment for the purposes of industrial injuries benefit` (JUST TRUE) NOTHING EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2(4) the employment is employed earner's employment for the purposes of industrial injuries benefit` NOTHING NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 2(5)
#ASSERT `s 2(5) the person is treated as a self-employed earner as respects the week` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2(5) the person is treated as a self-employed earner as respects the week` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `s 3`

#ASSERT `s 3(1)(a) the payment is earnings` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 3(1)(a) the payment is earnings` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 3(1)(b) the person is an earner` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 3(1)(b) the person is an earner` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `s 4`

-- s 4(1)(a): each of the seven listed kinds, with and without a sum paid in satisfaction of the entitlement
#ASSERT `s 4(1)(a) the sum is treated as remuneration derived from employed earner's employment` `statutory sick pay` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 4(1)(a) the sum is treated as remuneration derived from employed earner's employment` `statutory maternity pay` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 4(1)(a) the sum is treated as remuneration derived from employed earner's employment` `statutory paternity pay` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 4(1)(a) the sum is treated as remuneration derived from employed earner's employment` `statutory adoption pay` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 4(1)(a) the sum is treated as remuneration derived from employed earner's employment` `statutory shared parental pay` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 4(1)(a) the sum is treated as remuneration derived from employed earner's employment` `statutory parental bereavement pay` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 4(1)(a) the sum is treated as remuneration derived from employed earner's employment` `statutory neonatal care pay` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 4(1)(a) the sum is treated as remuneration derived from employed earner's employment` `statutory sick pay` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 4(1)(b): both limbs needed
#ASSERT `s 4(1)(b) the sickness payment is treated as remuneration derived from employed earner's employment` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 4(1)(b) the sickness payment is treated as remuneration derived from employed earner's employment` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 4(1)(b) the sickness payment is treated as remuneration derived from employed earner's employment` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 4(3)
#ASSERT `s 4(3) the payment is a sickness payment` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 4(3) the payment is a sickness payment` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 4(4)(a): gain 1000 less deductions 300 = 700; deductions equal to the gain = 0; deductions above the gain: not covered (fork F2)
#ASSERT `s 4(4)(a) the amount treated as remuneration derived from employed earner's employment` TRUE 1000 300 EQUALS JUST 700
#ASSERT `s 4(4)(a) the amount treated as remuneration derived from employed earner's employment` TRUE 1000 1000 EQUALS JUST 0
#ASSERT `s 4(4)(a) the amount treated as remuneration derived from employed earner's employment` TRUE 1000 1001 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 4(4)(a) the amount treated as remuneration derived from employed earner's employment` FALSE 1000 300 EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 4(4)(b)
#ASSERT `s 4(4)(b) the sum is treated as remuneration derived from an employed earner's employment` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 4(4)(b) the sum is treated as remuneration derived from an employed earner's employment` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 4(4)(b) the sum is treated as remuneration derived from an employed earner's employment` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 4(6C): an equivalent may exceed the arithmetical equivalent (100) by not more than 1
#ASSERT `s 4(6C)(b) the regulations may prescribe the amount as an equivalent of the contributions limit` 101 100 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 4(6C)(b) the regulations may prescribe the amount as an equivalent of the contributions limit` 100.5 100 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 4(6C)(b) the regulations may prescribe the amount as an equivalent of the contributions limit` 101.01 100 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 4(6C)(b) the regulations may prescribe the amount as an equivalent of the contributions limit` 100 100 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 4(6C)(b) the regulations may prescribe the amount as an equivalent of the contributions limit` 99 100 EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 4(6E)
#ASSERT `s 4(6E) the meaning of the expression in subsection (6A)` TRUE EQUALS JUST `s 4(6E) the meaning the expression has in the benefits code`
#ASSERT `s 4(6E) the meaning of the expression in subsection (6A)` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `s 4A`

#ASSERT `s 4A(1) the regulations may treat relevant payments or benefits as earnings paid to the worker in respect of an employed earner's employment` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 4A(1) the regulations may treat relevant payments or benefits as earnings paid to the worker in respect of an employed earner's employment` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 4A(1) the regulations may treat relevant payments or benefits as earnings paid to the worker in respect of an employed earner's employment` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 4A(1) the regulations may treat relevant payments or benefits as earnings paid to the worker in respect of an employed earner's employment` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 4A(2)(a): the third person if it has the specified relationship; else another person with both; else nobody
#ASSERT `s 4A(2)(a) who the intermediary is` TRUE TRUE EQUALS `s 4A(2)(a)(i) the third person`
#ASSERT `s 4A(2)(a) who the intermediary is` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `s 4A(2)(a)(i) the third person`
#ASSERT `s 4A(2)(a) who the intermediary is` FALSE TRUE EQUALS `s 4A(2)(a)(ii) another person who has both relationships`
#ASSERT `s 4A(2)(a) who the intermediary is` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `s 4A(2) nobody is the intermediary on these facts`
-- s 4A(2)(b)
#ASSERT `s 4A(2)(b) the person may be the intermediary despite being a person of the kind` `s 4A(2)(b)(i) a person with whom the worker holds any office or employment` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 4A(2)(b) the person may be the intermediary despite being a person of the kind` `s 4A(2)(b)(ii) a body corporate, unincorporated body or partnership of which the worker is a member` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 4A(2)(b) the person may be the intermediary despite being a person of the kind` `s 4A(2)(b) a person of another kind` EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 4A(2) closing words: whether or not, subsection (1) applies
#ASSERT `s 4A(2) subsection (1) applies whether or not the client is a person with whom the worker holds an office or employment` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 4A(2) subsection (1) applies whether or not the client is a person with whom the worker holds an office or employment` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- s 4A(3)(a)
#ASSERT `s 4A(3)(a) the worker's attributable earnings` 250 EQUALS 250
-- s 4A(6)
#ASSERT `s 4A(6) the Part is among the applicable provisions of this Act` `s 4A(6) Part I` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 4A(6) the Part is among the applicable provisions of this Act` `s 4A(6) Part II` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 4A(6) the Part is among the applicable provisions of this Act` `s 4A(6) Part V` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 4A(6) the Part is among the applicable provisions of this Act` `s 4A(6) a Part after Part V` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 4A(6) the activity carried on by the body is a business` `s 4A(6) a government department or public or local authority, in the United Kingdom or elsewhere` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 4A(6) the activity carried on by the body is a business` `s 4A(6) a body corporate, unincorporated body or partnership` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 4A(6) the activity carried on by the body is a business` `s 4A(6) a body of another kind` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 4A(6) the payments or benefits are relevant payments or benefits` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 4A(6) the payments or benefits are relevant payments or benefits` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 4A(6) the payments or benefits are relevant payments or benefits` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 4A(6) the description is specified` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 4A(6) the description is specified` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 4A(7)
#ASSERT `s 4A(7) the worker is treated as performing the services` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 4A(7) the worker is treated as performing the services` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 4A(7) the worker is treated as performing the services` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

